= The Typed Imp Language Specification
:toc: left
:toclevels: 2
:sectnums:
:icons: font

Typed Imp is a small typed imperative language. Its syntax covers
integer and boolean literals, variables, arithmetic and boolean
operators, sequencing, conditionals, `while` loops, and typed variable
declarations. The static semantics assigns types to expressions and
commands under a typing context; the dynamic semantics evaluates
expressions and executes commands under an environment that maps
variables to values.

== Syntax

The abstract syntax of Typed Imp distinguishes types, literals,
variables, expressions, commands, and whole programs.

[[type]]
[[literal]]
[[id]]
[[expr]]
[[command]]
[[prog]]
[source,bison]
----
syntax type = 
   | INT
   | BOOL
   | {type -> type}

syntax literal = 
   | {_NUM int}
   | {_BOOL bool}

syntax id = 
   | {_ID text}

syntax expr = 
   | literal
   | id
   | {! expr}
   | {expr + expr}
   | {expr <= expr}
   | {expr && expr}
   | {FUN `({type id}) -> type `{expr}}
   | {expr `(expr)}

syntax command = 
   | SKIP
   | {type id = expr}
   | {id = expr}
   | {IF expr THEN command ELSE command END}
   | {WHILE expr DO command END}
   | {command ; command}

syntax prog = command
----

== Auxiliary definitions

These auxiliary functions are shared by the static and dynamic
semantics.

=== Lookup

Lookup over an association list takes a list of `(key, value)` pairs and
returns the first value bound to the requested key.

[[lookup]]
[.sidebar-title]
****
xref:lookup[$lookup]<K, V>(pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^, K~query~)
****

[[lookup]]
****
xref:lookup[$lookup<K, V>(pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^, K~query~)]

. If ``pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Return ``·``.
. Else if let ``K~h~ → V~h~ {two-colons} ( K~t~ → V~t~ )^{asterisk}^`` be ``pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^``:
 .. Check that ``K~h~`` is equal to ``K~query~``.
 .. Return ``V~h~``.
. Otherwise:
 .. Check that ``pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^`` is a non-empty list.
 .. Let ``K~h~ → V~h~ {two-colons} ( K~t~ → V~t~ )^{asterisk}^`` be ``pair<K, V>^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Return ``xref:lookup[$lookup<K, V>(( K~t~ → V~t~ )^{asterisk}^, K~query~)]``.
****

=== Shorthands

[#option_get]
==== Force-unwrap (`?`)

Force-unwraps an optional. If the value is none, the rule does not apply.

[#subtype_check]
==== Subtype check (`<:`)

The value must belong to this subtype; otherwise the rule does not apply.

== Static semantics

The typing judgments characterise well-formed expressions and commands
under a typing context that maps each in-scope variable to its declared
type.

=== Expressions

[[Check_expr]]
[.sidebar-title]
****
xref:Check_expr[Check_expr: ``tenv ⊢ expr +++:+++ %``]
****

****
. If let ``literal`` be ``expr``:
 .. If let ``i`` be ``literal``:
  ... Result in ``+++INT+++``.
 .. Else if let ``b`` be ``literal``:
  ... Result in ``+++BOOL+++``.
. Else if let ``x`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let~xref:option_get[?]~ ``t`` be ``xref:lookup[$lookup<id, type>(tenv, x)]``.
 .. Result in ``t``.
. Else if let ``+++!+++ e`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e +++:+++ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+++BOOL+++``.
 .. Result in ``+++BOOL+++``.
. Else if let ``e~l~ +++++++ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~l~ +++:+++ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+++INT+++``.
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~r~ +++:+++ type'``].
 .. Check that ``type'`` matches pattern ``+++INT+++``.
 .. Result in ``+++INT+++``.
. Else if let ``e~l~ +++<=+++ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~l~ +++:+++ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+++INT+++``.
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~r~ +++:+++ type'``].
 .. Check that ``type'`` matches pattern ``+++INT+++``.
 .. Result in ``+++BOOL+++``.
. Else if let ``e~l~ +++&&+++ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~l~ +++:+++ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+++BOOL+++``.
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~r~ +++:+++ type'``].
 .. Check that ``type'`` matches pattern ``+++BOOL+++``.
 .. Result in ``+++BOOL+++``.
. Else if let ``+++FUN+++ +++(+++t~arg~ x~arg~+++)+++ +++->+++ t~ret~ +++{+++e+++}+++`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``x~arg~ → t~arg~ {two-colons} tenv ⊢ e +++:+++ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` is equal to ``t~ret~``.
 .. Result in ``t~arg~ +++->+++ t~ret~``.
. Else if let ``e~f~ +++(+++e~a~+++)+++`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~f~ +++:+++ type``].
 .. Let~xref:subtype_check[<:]~ ``t~arg~ +++->+++ t~ret~`` be ``type``.
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e~a~ +++:+++ type'``].
 .. Check that ``type'`` is equal to ``t~arg~``.
 .. Result in ``t~ret~``.
****

=== Commands

[[Check_command]]
[.sidebar-title]
****
xref:Check_command[Check_command: ``tenv ⊢ command ⊣ %``]
****

****
. If ``command`` matches pattern ``+++SKIP+++``:
 .. Result in ``tenv``.
. Else if let ``t x +++=+++ e`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e +++:+++ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` is equal to ``t``.
 .. Result in ``x → t {two-colons} tenv``.
. Else if let ``x +++=+++ e`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e +++:+++ t``].
 .. Check that ``xref:lookup[$lookup<id, type>(tenv, x)]`` is equal to ``t``.
 .. Result in ``tenv``.
. Else if let ``+++IF+++ e +++THEN+++ c~1~ +++ELSE+++ c~2~ +++END+++`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e +++:+++ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+++BOOL+++``.
 .. Let xref:Check_command[``tenv ⊢ c~1~ ⊣ tenv~1~``].
 .. Let xref:Check_command[``tenv ⊢ c~2~ ⊣ tenv~2~``].
 .. Result in ``tenv``.
. Else if let ``+++WHILE+++ e +++DO+++ c +++END+++`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Check_expr[``tenv ⊢ e +++:+++ type``].
 .. Check that ``type`` matches pattern ``+++BOOL+++``.
 .. Let xref:Check_command[``tenv ⊢ c ⊣ tenv~1~``].
 .. Result in ``tenv``.
. Else if let ``c~1~ +++;+++ c~2~`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Check_command[``tenv ⊢ c~1~ ⊣ tenv~1~``].
 .. Let xref:Check_command[``tenv~1~ ⊢ c~2~ ⊣ tenv~2~``].
 .. Result in ``tenv~2~``.
****

== Dynamic semantics

The evaluation judgments give a big-step semantics. Expressions reduce
to values; commands transform an environment to an environment.

=== Expressions

[[Eval_expr]]
[.sidebar-title]
****
xref:Eval_expr[Eval_expr: ``env ⊢ expr ⟹ %``]
****

****
. If let ``literal`` be ``expr``:
 .. If let ``i`` be ``literal``:
  ... Result in ``i``.
 .. Else if let ``b`` be ``literal``:
  ... Result in ``b``.
. Else if let ``x`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let~xref:option_get[?]~ ``v`` be ``xref:lookup[$lookup<id, value>(env, x)]``.
 .. Result in ``v``.
. Else if let ``+++!+++ e`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e ⟹ value``].
 .. Let~xref:subtype_check[<:]~ ``literal`` be ``value``.
 .. Let~xref:subtype_check[<:]~ ``b~e~`` be ``literal``.
 .. Let ``b`` be not ``b~e~``.
 .. Result in ``b``.
. Else if let ``e~l~ +++++++ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~l~ ⟹ value``].
 .. Let~xref:subtype_check[<:]~ ``literal`` be ``value``.
 .. Let~xref:subtype_check[<:]~ ``i~l~`` be ``literal``.
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~r~ ⟹ value'``].
 .. Let~xref:subtype_check[<:]~ ``literal'`` be ``value'``.
 .. Let~xref:subtype_check[<:]~ ``i~r~`` be ``literal'``.
 .. Let ``i`` be ``i~l~`` + ``i~r~``.
 .. Result in ``i``.
. Else if let ``e~l~ +++<=+++ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~l~ ⟹ value``].
 .. Let~xref:subtype_check[<:]~ ``literal`` be ``value``.
 .. Let~xref:subtype_check[<:]~ ``i~l~`` be ``literal``.
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~r~ ⟹ value'``].
 .. Let~xref:subtype_check[<:]~ ``literal'`` be ``value'``.
 .. Let~xref:subtype_check[<:]~ ``i~r~`` be ``literal'``.
 .. Let ``b`` be ``i~l~`` is less than or equal to ``i~r~``.
 .. Result in ``b``.
. Else if let ``e~l~ +++&&+++ e~r~`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~l~ ⟹ value``].
 .. Let~xref:subtype_check[<:]~ ``literal`` be ``value``.
 .. Let~xref:subtype_check[<:]~ ``b~l~`` be ``literal``.
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~r~ ⟹ value'``].
 .. Let~xref:subtype_check[<:]~ ``literal'`` be ``value'``.
 .. Let~xref:subtype_check[<:]~ ``b~r~`` be ``literal'``.
 .. Let ``b`` be ``b~l~`` and ``b~r~``.
 .. Result in ``b``.
. Else if let ``+++FUN+++ +++(+++t~arg~ x~arg~+++)+++ +++->+++ t~ret~ +++{+++e+++}+++`` be ``expr``:
 .. Result in ``+++CLO+++ x~arg~ e env``.
. Else if let ``e~f~ +++(+++e~a~+++)+++`` be ``expr``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~f~ ⟹ value``].
 .. Let~xref:subtype_check[<:]~ ``+++CLO+++ x~a~ e~body~ env~clo~`` be ``value``.
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e~a~ ⟹ v``].
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``x~a~ → v {two-colons} env~clo~ ⊢ e~body~ ⟹ v~ret~``].
 .. Result in ``v~ret~``.
****

=== Commands

[[Eval_command]]
[.sidebar-title]
****
xref:Eval_command[Eval_command: ``env ⊢ command ⊣ %``]
****

****
. If ``command`` matches pattern ``+++SKIP+++``:
 .. Result in ``env``.
. Else if let ``t x +++=+++ e`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e ⟹ v``].
 .. Result in ``x → v {two-colons} env``.
. Else if let ``x +++=+++ e`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e ⟹ v``].
 .. Result in ``x → v {two-colons} env``.
. Else if let ``+++IF+++ e +++THEN+++ c~1~ +++ELSE+++ c~2~ +++END+++`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e ⟹ value``].
 .. If ``value`` is equal to ``true``:
  ... Let xref:Eval_command[``env ⊢ c~1~ ⊣ env~1~``].
  ... Result in ``env~1~``.
 .. Else if ``value`` is equal to ``false``:
  ... Let xref:Eval_command[``env ⊢ c~2~ ⊣ env~2~``].
  ... Result in ``env~2~``.
. Else if let ``+++WHILE+++ e +++DO+++ c +++END+++`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_expr[``env ⊢ e ⟹ value``].
 .. If ``value`` is equal to ``false``:
  ... Result in ``env``.
 .. Else if ``value`` is equal to ``true``:
  ... Let xref:Eval_command[``env ⊢ c ⊣ env~1~``].
  ... Let xref:Eval_command[``env~1~ ⊢ +++WHILE+++ e +++DO+++ c +++END+++ ⊣ env~2~``].
  ... Result in ``env~2~``.
. Else if let ``c~1~ +++;+++ c~2~`` be ``command``:
 .. Let xref:Eval_command[``env ⊢ c~1~ ⊣ env~1~``].
 .. Let xref:Eval_command[``env~1~ ⊢ c~2~ ⊣ env~2~``].
 .. Result in ``env~2~``.
****
